# ivtest expected-failures list — consumed by .github/ivtest_gate.sh
# One test name per line; everything after the name is commentary.
# RULES (manifesto Phase 0): a test may only appear here with a
# written reason, and the gate fails BOTH on unexplained new failures
# and on stale entries. Full attribution: ivtest_vendored_baseline_*.txt
# and test_suite_audit_2026-07-17.md.
#
# --- Pre-existing upstream failures: NONE (was 31).
# --- The 2026-07-28 deep investigation found 29 of the 31 were verdict
# --- convention artifacts (the tests printed "PASS"; gold-less normal
# --- tests require the literal string "PASSED") and ran clean;
# --- sv_class_static_queue_pop_back used silence-as-success (no verdict
# --- print at all); sv_uarray_locator1 used `return' directly in an
# --- initial block, which is illegal (IEEE 1800-2017 13.4.4), so
# --- rejecting it was conformant -- the legal form passes. All 31
# --- tests were repaired and are now actively enforced.
#
# --- Documented fork divergences (3 remaining -- the br trio).
# --- 2026-07-28 closure pass: case_unique,
# --- struct_invalid_member and the timeunit pair were regolded to
# --- LRM-correct output (5.7.1 digit separators made `1_0s` legal, so
# --- the correct diagnostic became the 3.14.2 repeat-mismatch);
# --- R28 turned sv_class_new_fail1 + func_empty_arg_fail4 into real
# --- diagnostics; and the deferred assert/assume quartet's ledger
# --- reason was FALSE -- the fork never implemented deferred
# --- assertions, it silently DELETED them (parser nulled the statement
# --- and the fork's flag defaults suppressed upstream's sorry).
# --- Restoring the upstream defaults makes them a loud sorry again,
# --- which is exactly what those four golds expect (R29 tracks the
# --- real 16.4 implementation). All ten now pass, actively enforced:
br1005		# implemented-feature divergence: fork legalizes queue-in-class (gold expects rejection)
br_ml20150315b		# implemented-feature divergence: fork legalizes the declaration form (gold expects rejection)
br_ml20180227		# implemented-feature divergence: fork legalizes the assignment form (gold expects rejection)
